Round 7 (2026-02-26)

What changed this round (landed)
- Landed code changes in:
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
- Added strict-site deopt metadata plumbing (source-mapped by static term loc):
  - New `AotDeoptSiteKind` enum:
    - `AOT_DEOPT_SITE_KIND_HEAD_SWI_NON_NUM`
    - `AOT_DEOPT_SITE_KIND_HEAD_MAT_NON_CTR`
  - New runtime metadata arrays keyed by deopt site id:
    - kind, static loc, aux (expected case ext).
  - New runtime API: `aot_deopt_site_define(site, kind, loc, aux)`.
  - `aot_deopt_dump(stderr)` top-sites now prints metadata when present:
    - `kind=... loc=... expect_num=...` or `expect_ctr_ext=...`.
- Emitter now stores per-site metadata while assigning site ids and emits:
  - `aot_register_deopt_sites_generated()` in generated C,
  - called from generated `main()` before eval.
- Head strict mismatch emission change:
  - In compiled head `SWI`: `arg` non-NUM now returns direct fallback with metadata kind `HEAD_SWI_NON_NUM`.
  - In compiled head `MAT`: scrutinee non-CTR-tag now returns direct fallback with metadata kind `HEAD_MAT_NON_CTR`.
  - Reason stays `AOT_DEOPT_EXPR_UNSUPPORTED_TAG` for continuity of existing counters.

Why this was done
- `EXPR_UNSUPPORTED_TAG` remained dominant and opaque in `gab_tak`/`gab_takl`.
- We need exact hotspot attribution (strict site kind + static loc + expected class/ext) before retrying any strict forcing redesign.

